{"id":"john-muir-trail","title":"John Muir Trail","who":"Classic route · the High Sierra, California","when":"July to September","vehicle":"On foot, 2–3 weeks (permits by lottery)","kind":"walk","color":"#4338ca","summary":"About 340 km from Yosemite Valley to the summit of Mount Whitney, the highest point in the lower 48: granite domes, a dozen passes over 3,300 m, Evolution Basin's lakes, Muir Pass's stone hut, and almost no roads. Shares much of its way with the Pacific Crest Trail.","sources":[{"label":"FarOut: reflections from the John Muir Trail (2025)","url":"https://faroutguides.com/reflections-from-the-john-muir-trail/"},{"label":"Halfway Anywhere: John Muir Trail, class of 2025","url":"https://www.halfwayanywhere.com/trails/john-muir-trail/jmt-hiker-surprises-2025/"}],"approximate":"Main points; the line follows trails where they were found.","km":253,"bbox":[-119.5582,36.5785,-118.2923,37.8797],"stops":[{"name":"Happy Isles","place":"Happy Isles, Yosemite","at":[37.7316,-119.5575],"text":"The start in Yosemite Valley, up past Vernal and Nevada falls.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Tunnel_View%2C_Yosemite_Valley%2C_Yosemite_NP_-_Diliff.jpg/500px-Tunnel_View%2C_Yosemite_Valley%2C_Yosemite_NP_-_Diliff.jpg","page":"Yosemite Valley","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tunnel_View%2C_Yosemite_Valley%2C_Yosemite_NP_-_Diliff.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Tuolumne Meadows","place":"Tuolumne Meadows","at":[37.8795,-119.3866],"text":"Over Cathedral Pass to the high meadows.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Tuolumne_Meadows_Sunset.jpg/500px-Tuolumne_Meadows_Sunset.jpg","page":"Tuolumne Meadows","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tuolumne_Meadows_Sunset.jpg","credit":"Steve Dunleavy from Lake Tahoe, NV, United States","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Thousand Island Lake","place":"Thousand Island Lake","at":[37.7225,-119.1797],"text":"Over Donohue Pass, Banner Peak above a lake of islets.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Mt_Banner_and_Thousand_Island_Lake.jpg/500px-Mt_Banner_and_Thousand_Island_Lake.jpg","page":"Thousand Island Lake","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mt_Banner_and_Thousand_Island_Lake.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Reds Meadow","place":"Reds Meadow","at":[37.6158,-119.0744],"text":"The basalt columns of Devils Postpile; resupply.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Devils_Postpile_National_Monument_near_Mammoth_Lakes.jpg/500px-Devils_Postpile_National_Monument_near_Mammoth_Lakes.jpg","page":"Devils Postpile National Monument","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devils_Postpile_National_Monument_near_Mammoth_Lakes.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Muir Trail Ranch","place":"Muir Trail Ranch","at":[37.2431,-118.8828],"text":"A remote ranch that holds hikers' resupply buckets.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Long_Lake_in_Little_Lakes_Valley.jpg/500px-Long_Lake_in_Little_Lakes_Valley.jpg","page":"John Muir Wilderness","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Long_Lake_in_Little_Lakes_Valley.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Evolution Basin","place":"Evolution Lake","at":[37.1633,-118.7072],"text":"Lakes under peaks named after Darwin and Huxley: many hikers' favourite day.","source":{"label":"FarOut (2025)","url":"https://faroutguides.com/reflections-from-the-john-muir-trail/"}},{"name":"Muir Pass","place":"Muir Hut","at":[37.1119,-118.6706],"text":"The stone hut on top of the pass, 3,644 m.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Muir_Pass.jpg/500px-Muir_Pass.jpg","page":"Muir Pass","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muir_Pass.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Rae Lakes","place":"Rae Lakes","at":[36.8131,-118.4011],"text":"Over Mather, Pinchot and Glen passes to one of the Sierra's loveliest lakes."},{"name":"Forester Pass","place":"Forester Pass","at":[36.6942,-118.3717],"text":"The highest pass on the trail, 4,009 m."},{"name":"Mount Whitney","place":"Mount Whitney","at":[36.5785,-118.2923],"text":"The summit at 4,421 m, then down to Whitney Portal.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Mount_Whitney_2003-03-25.jpg/500px-Mount_Whitney_2003-03-25.jpg","page":"Mount Whitney","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Whitney_2003-03-25.jpg","credit":"Geographer (talk · contribs)","license":"CC BY 1.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"walk","km":34,"line":[[37.7318,-119.5582],[37.7262,-119.5568],[37.7261,-119.5304],[37.7354,-119.514],[37.7451,-119.5127],[37.7437,-119.4971],[37.7586,-119.4761],[37.7613,-119.4541],[37.7962,-119.429],[37.811,-119.4295],[37.822,-119.418],[37.839,-119.4118],[37.8515,-119.4149],[37.8616,-119.4061],[37.871,-119.3846],[37.8778,-119.3953],[37.8797,-119.3887]]},{"by":"walk","km":25,"line":[[37.8795,-119.3866],[37.7225,-119.1797]]},{"by":"walk","km":21,"line":[[37.7256,-119.1827],[37.7328,-119.1637],[37.7097,-119.1278],[37.6783,-119.0962],[37.6716,-119.0812],[37.666,-119.0767],[37.6545,-119.0802],[37.6514,-119.0744],[37.6159,-119.0741]]},{"by":"walk","km":80,"line":[[37.6159,-119.0741],[37.605,-119.0723],[37.604,-119.0635],[37.5944,-119.0619],[37.5987,-119.0608],[37.5906,-119.0582],[37.5731,-119.0402],[37.5525,-119.0311],[37.5467,-119.0054],[37.5496,-118.9985],[37.5357,-118.9813],[37.539,-118.9703],[37.5243,-118.9635],[37.5275,-118.946],[37.5065,-118.9283],[37.5063,-118.9216],[37.4836,-118.9369],[37.4776,-118.9242],[37.475,-118.9294],[37.4725,-118.9231],[37.4581,-118.9185],[37.4442,-118.9232],[37.4363,-118.9075],[37.4177,-118.9116],[37.4083,-118.9308],[37.4012,-118.927],[37.3963,-118.9303],[37.3658,-118.8846],[37.3